{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
  "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Digital Realty Trust, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHANMUGAM: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Dodd-Frank Act provides incentives to and protections for whistleblowers; that is, individuals who have reported securities law violations to the SEC."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about employees who must report internally before they can report to the SEC?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Official question about the ordinary meaning of whistleblower."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our submission, our core submission to the Court is this is a simple case that can be resolved at step 1 of Chevron, the terms and reach of the statutory definition are unambiguous and there's certainly no absurdity here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent relies on section, I believe it's 2401, which is the general six-year limitations period for claims against the government. That is a limitations period that is applicable in ordinary APA actions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Is every employee obligated by law to report a violation or is it only certain employees, lawyers and accountants and others who are affirmatively obligated to report?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, no, but I mean I asked that -- first, I want you to answer Justice Gorsuch's question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the logical outgrowth test, is -- is it anticipated that something is going to follow? Is it reasonable notice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I just ask whether Somers -- was there any reason he didn't report to the SEC?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher G. Michel",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statutory definition of whistleblower is tailor-made for the awards program, but it does not fit in the retaliation programs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, Mr. Michel, I do think that that's a real anomaly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"Who provides information to the Commission.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Bottom line, are you -- how much are you relying on just Chevron deference here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0002-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You only give it if they report to the SEC?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1276",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d8f948fc398690a4e1054fb73a0dc3242c6ccffc3b45b6d28dd23ff056f08e81",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d8f948fc3986-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:07 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
